# PowerPoint for Git Repos

this is meant to be a dotnet tool that allows you to:

also, thinking of a way of rendering pptx to a long png of the slides. The idea would be for a pptx with 4 commits, there would be a corrospanding my.pptx.coomithash.preview.png that would be .gitignored, but allow diffing on your computer. might even retroactively create if needed.


usage

```bash
CreatePowerpointCheckpoint file.pptx # create the png for the last commit it was edited in
CreatePowerpointCheckpoint file.pptx --commit sha1,sha2,sha3 # create 3 png
CreatePowerpointCheckpoint file.pptx --compare sha1 sha2
CreatePowerpointCheckpoint file.pptx --compare  # creates a temp commit if it has been edited but not commited and then compares last edited
CreatePowerpointCheckpoint file.pptx --compare sha1  # creates a temp commit if it has been edited but not commited and then compares againist sh1

``` 

